# ── Cell 1: Config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
from ultralytics import YOLO
from pathlib import Path
from IPython.display import display, Markdown
import numpy as np
import cv2
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import matplotlib.patches as mpatches

MODEL_PATH  = "your_finetuned_model.pt"
TRACKER     = "custom_botsort.yaml"
MIN_CONF    = 0.3       # lowest conf to consider — below this is noise
VALID_LABELS = {"soldier", "civilian"}

VAL_VIDEOS = [
    "val_video_1.mp4",
    "val_video_2.mp4",
    "val_video_3.mp4",
    "val_video_4.mp4",
    "val_video_5.mp4",
    "val_video_6.mp4",
    "val_video_7.mp4",
    "val_video_8.mp4",
]


# ── Cell 2: Run tracking on all validation videos ──────────────────────────────
model      = YOLO(MODEL_PATH)
all_tracks = {}  # (video_id, track_id) → stats

for video_path in VAL_VIDEOS:
    video_id = Path(video_path).stem
    print(f"\nProcessing {video_id}...")

    results = model.track(
        source=video_path,
        tracker=TRACKER,
        conf=MIN_CONF,
        iou=0.5,
        stream=True,
        persist=True,
    )

    for frame_idx, result in enumerate(results):
        if result.boxes is None or result.boxes.id is None:
            continue

        for i in range(len(result.boxes)):
            label    = result.names[int(result.boxes.cls[i].item())]
            if label not in VALID_LABELS:
                continue

            track_id = int(result.boxes.id[i].item())
            conf     = result.boxes.conf[i].item()
            key      = (video_id, track_id)

            if key not in all_tracks:
                all_tracks[key] = {
                    "confs":     [],
                    "labels":    [],
                    "frame_ids": [],
                    "video_id":  video_id,
                    "track_id":  track_id,
                }

            all_tracks[key]["confs"].append(conf)
            all_tracks[key]["labels"].append(label)
            all_tracks[key]["frame_ids"].append(frame_idx)

    print(f"  Tracks so far: {len(all_tracks)}")

# Compute stats per track
for key, t in all_tracks.items():
    confs    = t["confs"]
    labels   = t["labels"]
    majority = "soldier" if labels.count("soldier") >= len(labels) / 2 else "civilian"
    is_mixed = "soldier" in labels and "civilian" in labels

    t["mean_conf"]         = round(np.mean(confs), 4)
    t["conf_std"]          = round(np.std(confs),  4)
    t["max_conf"]          = round(np.max(confs),  4)
    t["min_conf"]          = round(np.min(confs),  4)
    t["label_consistency"] = round(labels.count(majority) / len(labels), 4)
    t["majority_label"]    = majority
    t["is_mixed"]          = is_mixed
    t["n_frames"]          = len(confs)

display(Markdown(f"""
## Tracking complete
| | |
|---|---|
| Total tracks | {len(all_tracks)} |
| Soldier tracks | {sum(1 for t in all_tracks.values() if t['majority_label'] == 'soldier')} |
| Civilian tracks | {sum(1 for t in all_tracks.values() if t['majority_label'] == 'civilian')} |
| Mixed label tracks | {sum(1 for t in all_tracks.values() if t['is_mixed'])} |
"""))


# ── Cell 3: Visualize tracks for manual ground truth labeling ──────────────────
# Run this cell to review tracks and fill in ground_truth dict below

def show_track(key, track, n_frames=6):
    video_id, track_id = key
    cap = cv2.VideoCapture(f"{video_id}.mp4")

    frame_ids = track["frame_ids"]
    step      = max(1, len(frame_ids) // n_frames)
    sample    = frame_ids[::step][:n_frames]

    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(sample), figsize=(16, 3))
    if len(sample) == 1:
        axes = [axes]

    fig.suptitle(
        f"{video_id} | track {track_id} | majority={track['majority_label']} | "
        f"mixed={track['is_mixed']} | mean_conf={track['mean_conf']:.2f} | "
        f"std={track['conf_std']:.2f} | consistency={track['label_consistency']:.2f} | "
        f"n_frames={track['n_frames']}",
        fontsize=9
    )

    for ax, fid in zip(axes, sample):
        cap.set(cv2.CAP_PROP_POS_FRAMES, fid)
        ret, frame = cap.read()
        if ret:
            ax.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(frame, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))
            ax.set_title(f"f{fid}", fontsize=8)
        ax.axis("off")

    cap.release()
    plt.tight_layout()
    plt.show()

# Show all tracks for labeling
for key, track in all_tracks.items():
    show_track(key, track)


# ── Cell 4: Enter ground truth here after reviewing tracks ─────────────────────
# Fill this in after running Cell 3
# Format: {("video_stem", track_id): "soldier" | "civilian"}

ground_truth = {
    # ("val_video_1", 1): "soldier",
    # ("val_video_1", 2): "civilian",
    # ("val_video_2", 1): "soldier",
    # ... add all tracks here
}


# ── Cell 5: Split tracks into categories ──────────────────────────────────────
labeled = {k: t for k, t in all_tracks.items() if k in ground_truth}

correct_soldier    = [t for k, t in labeled.items()
                      if ground_truth[k] == "soldier"
                      and t["majority_label"] == "soldier"
                      and not t["is_mixed"]]

missed_soldier     = [t for k, t in labeled.items()
                      if ground_truth[k] == "soldier"
                      and t["majority_label"] == "civilian"
                      and not t["is_mixed"]]

correct_civilian   = [t for k, t in labeled.items()
                      if ground_truth[k] == "civilian"
                      and t["majority_label"] == "civilian"
                      and not t["is_mixed"]]

false_soldier      = [t for k, t in labeled.items()
                      if ground_truth[k] == "civilian"
                      and t["majority_label"] == "soldier"
                      and not t["is_mixed"]]

mixed_true_soldier  = [t for k, t in labeled.items()
                       if ground_truth[k] == "soldier"
                       and t["is_mixed"]]

mixed_true_civilian = [t for k, t in labeled.items()
                       if ground_truth[k] == "civilian"
                       and t["is_mixed"]]

display(Markdown(f"""
## Track categories
| Category | Count |
|---|---|
| Correct soldier (pure) | {len(correct_soldier)} |
| Missed soldier (called civilian) | {len(missed_soldier)} |
| Correct civilian (pure) | {len(correct_civilian)} |
| False soldier (civilian called soldier) | {len(false_soldier)} |
| Mixed → actually soldier | {len(mixed_true_soldier)} |
| Mixed → actually civilian | {len(mixed_true_civilian)} |
"""))


# ── Cell 6: Plot metric distributions ─────────────────────────────────────────
metrics = [
    ("mean_conf",         "Mean Confidence"),
    ("conf_std",          "Confidence Std"),
    ("label_consistency", "Label Consistency"),
    ("max_conf",          "Max Confidence"),
]

categories = [
    (correct_soldier,     "correct soldier",     "green"),
    (missed_soldier,      "missed soldier",      "red"),
    (correct_civilian,    "correct civilian",    "blue"),
    (false_soldier,       "false soldier alarm", "orange"),
    (mixed_true_soldier,  "mixed → soldier",     "darkgreen"),
    (mixed_true_civilian, "mixed → civilian",    "purple"),
]

fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(16, 12))
axes = axes.flatten()

for col, (metric, title) in enumerate(metrics):
    ax = axes[col]
    for tracks_list, label, color in categories:
        vals = [t[metric] for t in tracks_list]
        if vals:
            ax.hist(vals, bins=20, alpha=0.5, color=color, label=label)

    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=12)
    ax.set_xlabel("Value")
    ax.set_ylabel("Count")
    ax.legend(fontsize=8)

    # Print stats per category
    print(f"\n{title}:")
    for tracks_list, label, _ in categories:
        vals = [t[metric] for t in tracks_list]
        if vals:
            print(f"  {label:30s}: mean={np.mean(vals):.3f}  std={np.std(vals):.3f}  "
                  f"min={np.min(vals):.3f}  max={np.max(vals):.3f}")

plt.tight_layout()
plt.show()


# ── Cell 7: Find threshold that minimises missed soldiers ──────────────────────
# For each metric, find the value that catches the most missed soldiers
# while keeping false alarms manageable

display(Markdown("## Threshold analysis — minimising missed soldiers"))

for metric, title in metrics:
    missed_vals  = [t[metric] for t in missed_soldier + mixed_true_soldier]
    correct_vals = [t[metric] for t in correct_soldier]

    if not missed_vals or not correct_vals:
        continue

    # Try thresholds across the range
    all_vals   = [t[metric] for t in labeled.values()]
    thresholds = np.linspace(min(all_vals), max(all_vals), 50)

    best_thresh  = None
    best_recall  = 0
    results_rows = []

    for thresh in thresholds:
        # "send to Qwen if below threshold" logic for mean_conf/max_conf
        # "send to Qwen if above threshold" logic for conf_std
        if metric in ("mean_conf", "max_conf", "label_consistency"):
            send_to_qwen = lambda t: t[metric] < thresh
        else:  # conf_std — high std = send to Qwen
            send_to_qwen = lambda t: t[metric] > thresh

        # How many missed soldiers would be caught
        caught  = sum(1 for t in missed_soldier + mixed_true_soldier if send_to_qwen(t))
        total_missed = len(missed_soldier) + len(mixed_true_soldier)
        recall  = caught / total_missed if total_missed > 0 else 0

        # How many total tracks sent to Qwen (cost)
        total_sent = sum(1 for t in labeled.values() if send_to_qwen(t))
        cost_pct   = total_sent / len(labeled) * 100

        results_rows.append((thresh, recall, cost_pct))

        if recall > best_recall:
            best_recall = recall
            best_thresh = thresh

    # Plot recall vs cost
    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4))
    recalls   = [r[1] for r in results_rows]
    costs     = [r[2] for r in results_rows]
    threshs   = [r[0] for r in results_rows]

    ax.plot(threshs, recalls, color="red",  label="soldier recall (caught/total missed)")
    ax.plot(threshs, [c/100 for c in costs], color="blue", label="% tracks sent to Qwen")
    ax.axvline(best_thresh, color="green", linestyle="--",
               label=f"best threshold = {best_thresh:.3f}")
    ax.set_title(f"{title} — recall vs Qwen cost")
    ax.set_xlabel(metric)
    ax.legend()
    plt.tight_layout()
    plt.show()

    print(f"\n{title} — best threshold: {best_thresh:.3f}")
    print(f"  Catches {best_recall*100:.1f}% of missed soldiers")
    print(f"  Sends {costs[list(threshs).index(min(threshs, key=lambda x: abs(x-best_thresh)))]:,.1f}% of tracks to Qwen")


